  "$f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}x^{3/2}$, teda $f'(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ a $\\sqrt{1+f'^2(x)}=\\sqrt{1+x}$. $\\ell=\\displaystyle\\int_0^{{@0}}\\sqrt{1+x}\\,dx=\\frac{2}{3}\\left[(1+x)^{3/2}\\right]_0^{{@1}}=\\frac{2}{3}\\left({@2}^{3/2}-1\\right)=\\frac{2}{3}({@3}-1)={@4}$.": "$f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}x^{3/2}$, also $f'(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ und $\\sqrt{1+f'^2(x)}=\\sqrt{1+x}$. $\\ell=\\displaystyle\\int_0^{{@0}}\\sqrt{1+x}\\,dx=\\frac{2}{3}\\left[(1+x)^{3/2}\\right]_0^{{@1}}=\\frac{2}{3}\\left({@2}^{3/2}-1\\right)=\\frac{2}{3}({@3}-1)={@4}$.",
