  "$u=\\ln x$, $v'={@0}$, teda $u'=\\frac{1}{x}$, $v=\\frac{x^{{@1}}}{{@2}}$: $\\int {@3}\\ln x\\,dx=\\frac{x^{{@4}}}{{@5}}\\ln x-\\int\\frac{{@6}}{{@7}}\\,dx=\\frac{x^{{@8}}}{{@9}}\\ln x-\\frac{x^{{@10}}}{{@11}}+C$.": "$u=\\ln x$, $v'={@0}$, also $u'=\\frac{1}{x}$, $v=\\frac{x^{{@1}}}{{@2}}$: $\\int {@3}\\ln x\\,dx=\\frac{x^{{@4}}}{{@5}}\\ln x-\\int\\frac{{@6}}{{@7}}\\,dx=\\frac{x^{{@8}}}{{@9}}\\ln x-\\frac{x^{{@10}}}{{@11}}+C$.",
